5c628100743ba20b3589c6e3","file":"preprints/The-normalized-volume-gap-in-dimension-four-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex","line":74,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"11bea8415791b9d5e25b4a0d4b7b909687041714575628cb845c0b9abad7cd92","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-normalized-volume-gap-in-dimension-four-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:85629d1ec3a17691b78e6966d4af9c8470fc17a25c628100743ba20b3589c6e3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-normalized-volume-gap-in-dimension-four-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex#L74"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet \\(x\\in X\\) be a singular closed point of a normal complex algebraic variety of dimension four. Suppose that \\(K_X\\) is \\(\\Q\\)-Cartier and that \\(X\\) is klt near \\(x\\), with boundary zero. Then\n\\[\n\\nvol(x,X)\\le 162.\n\\]\nEquality holds if and only if the analytic germ \\((X,x)\\) is isomorphic to\n\\[\n\\left(\\left\\{z_0^2+z_1^2+z_2^2+z_3^2+z_4^2=0\\right\\}\\subset\\C^5,0\\right).\n\\]"}
